    {
      "id": "2122961773573894194",
      "text": "Collin Sexton made a good point that players with the hot hand can often shoot themselves out of it by taking bad shots. He credited Quentin Grimes for not forcing the issue and making sure he was taking good shots down the stretch to stay hot.",
